3.reversed(), that allow easy reversal of vector components. These methods multiply the x, y, and z components of the vectors by -1, effectively flipping the direction of the vector.\r\n\r\nWhy this is useful: These methods simplify vector manipulation when you need to reverse a vector quickly. This can be useful in various situations, such as inverting directions, or for physics and game mechanics where vectors may need to be flipped.\r\n\r\nUsage Example in GDScript:\r\n\r\nvar vec2 = Vector2(8, 9)\r\nvec2.reversed()\r\nprint(vec2)  # Output: (-8, -9)\r\nThis PR aims to enhance the utility of Vector2 and Vector3 classes with a simple yet effective method to reverse vector components.","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-04-14T12:01:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T12:14:59Z","closed_at":"2025-04-14T12:14:07Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"46c4ba2e8755ab7916d3882a5034072b82e1d17a","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":null,"ref":"vector_reversed","repo":null,"sha":"7d8229413b1c37483cb586ce4071a6b3507b8216","user":null},"base":{"label":"godotengine:master","ref":"master","repo":{"id":15634981,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxNTYzNDk4MQ==","name":"godot","full_name":"godoten